    docs: quote the check-binary-fresh guard messages verbatim. Addresses OB-GAP-076.
    
    Closes the GitReins Tier 2 judge's third and only remaining clause on OB-GAP-076,
    which returned INCOMPLETE. Clauses 1 and 2 already passed at c684c4c: every live
    build instruction now uses make build (docs/integration.md, docs/landing-spec.md,
    docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md, skills/off-by-one-usage/SKILL.md, README.md) and the
    only surviving bare go build ./cmd/off-by-one is the dated dogfood log
    docs/dogfood/2026-08-10-integration.md:83, which is historical and allowed. The
    judge's remaining objection was that no live doc quoted the guard's actual failure
    messages, so the criterion's explicit requirement was unmet. This commit adds them
    to the live docs that explain how to build and verify a build.
    
    The three quoted strings were extracted programmatically from the Makefile
    check-binary-fresh target (lines 50, 74 and 82), with the BINARY variable resolved
    to ./off-by-one and the stamp shell variable rendered as the placeholder <stamp>,
    rather than transcribed by hand. A comparison script asserts the quoted messages
    are byte-identical to the Makefile's own strings, so no paraphrase or invented
    variant is present.
    
    Docs only, three files:
    
    - docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md -- the step 4 "Test locally" item now also runs make
      check-binary-fresh and quotes all three failures verbatim, plus the shared remedy.
    - skills/off-by-one-usage/SKILL.md -- new "Binary-freshness guard" paragraph after
      the OB-GAP-062 deploy-lag trap carrying the same three messages.
    - README.md -- the "Rebuild after pulling" note now quotes the no-version-stamp
      message as emitted for a binary produced by a bare go build.
    
    No source, Makefile, AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, board, .gitreins or data changes;
    the gocmd build path line and the repo-wide build-all instructions are untouched.
    make build was deliberately NOT run in the repo, so the deployed ./off-by-one keeps
    its stamp and make check-binary-fresh still passes. Gates: go build ./... clean,
    go vet ./... clean, gofmt -l cmd/ internal/ pkg/ sql/ empty.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
